<header><p class="st-kicker">colony · Mesoamerica and the Caribbean</p><h1 class="st-title">Colony of the Bahamas</h1><p class="st-meta">1648 CE – 1973 CE · capital Nassau</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">British island colony that began as a refuge for Puritan dissenters, became a notorious pirate haven, and grew into the independent Commonwealth of The Bahamas.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 1648 the Eleutheran Adventurers, Puritan settlers from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bermuda">Bermuda</a> led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-sayle">William Sayle</a>, founded a colony on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eleuthera">Eleuthera</a>. Settlement spread to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-providence">New Providence</a>, where <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-nassau">Nassau</a> grew up. In 1670 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-ii-of-england">Charles II</a> granted the islands to the Lords Proprietors of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/province-of-carolina">Carolina</a>, whose weak rule left Nassau open to Spanish raids and, by the early 18th century, to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piracy">pirates</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The crown took direct control in 1718, when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/woodes-rogers">Woodes Rogers</a> arrived as royal governor and suppressed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piracy">pirates</a>; an elected House of Assembly followed in 1729. Loyalists from the American colonies arrived after 1783 with enslaved workers to plant <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cotton">cotton</a>, which soon failed. Wrecking, salt raking, sponging and later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naval-blockade">blockade</a> running in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-civil-war">American Civil War</a> and rum running during <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prohibition-in-the-united-states">Prohibition</a> sustained the economy. A small white merchant elite, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bay-street-boys">Bay Street Boys</a>, dominated politics.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Internal self-government came in 1964, and majority rule followed in 1967 under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lynden-pindling">Lynden Pindling's</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/progressive-liberal-party">Progressive Liberal Party</a>, after a long campaign by the black majority. The colony became independent as the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/bahamas">Bahamas</a> on 10 July 1973, by then reliant on tourism and offshore finance.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/colony-of-the-bahamas.jpg" alt="Colony of the Bahamas" width="320" height="160"><figcaption>Image: JackintheBox · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Bahamas_(1904%E2%80%931923)_with_text_removed.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1648 CE – 1973 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>colony</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Nassau</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>William Sayle, Woodes Rogers</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Protestantism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>English</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/bahamas">Bahamas</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>British Bahamas, Eleutheran Adventurers</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1810&amp;focus=colony-of-the-bahamas" aria-label="Colony of the Bahamas on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="2629 1255 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Colony of the Bahamas lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M2949 1511L2949 1511M2949 1511L4997 651M2949 1511L2949 1511M2949 1511L3090 1640"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M2949 1511h0M4997 651h0M2949 1511h0M3090 1640h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M2949 1511h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M2949 1511h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Nassau. <a href="/atlas?year=1810&amp;focus=colony-of-the-bahamas">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
